# Copy to hermes.env and fill in a model/provider so Hermes can actually
# converse on the call. Without a provider key the harness still validates the
# full SIP plumbing (register → Stasis → externalMedia → AudioSocket → STT),
# but the agent turn will fail at the LLM call.
#
# Any provider Hermes supports works; below is Nous Portal / OpenAI-style.
# See website/docs/user-guide/configuration for the full list.

# --- Model provider (pick one) ---
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=...
# NOUS_API_KEY=...

# --- Speech-to-text (inbound caller audio → text) ---
# Local faster-whisper needs no key (bundled with the [voice] extra); or use a
# cloud STT provider:
# GROQ_API_KEY=...
# OPENAI_API_KEY=...          # also used for Whisper STT / OpenAI TTS

# --- Text-to-speech (agent reply → spoken audio) ---
# ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=...      # or rely on the OpenAI/edge-tts defaults
